
The cell printed `r.stdout or r.stderr` and never checked the return code,
so a failed clone showed nothing useful -- IPython's bare "To exit: use
'exit'" warning from the SystemExit was all the user saw, with no indication
of why git failed.

Now always prints the exit code, stdout and stderr, checks returncode
explicitly, and names the usual cause (Internet disabled on Kaggle) with the
fix. Hiding a subprocess's stderr is exactly the wrong tradeoff at a step
that fails for environmental reasons.

Also made build_kaggle_nb.py write relative to its own location rather than
a hardcoded Windows path.

Verified both branches: a bad URL surfaces "Repository not found" then the
guidance (exit 1), and the real public repo clones and chdirs cleanly
(exit 0) -- which also confirms the repository is publicly reachable.

